              "title": "Cover the zero-diff bypass's rejection, fallback, and stale-target branches",
              "details": "The only runAutoreviewForTarget test exercises the successful trusted bypass. It does not prove that a nonqualifying snapshot delegates to the normal medium/high protocol, that invalid actor/tree/ancestry/path evidence cannot bypass review, or that a changed second read raises stale_target without publishing success. These are newly changed runtime and trust-boundary branches, so the trusted repository rule requiring tests for every changed runtime or policy branch is not satisfied.",
